# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values for the backend you actually run:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Only ONE backend block should be active at a time, and it must match the
# connector exported from kitcommerce.config.ts (and installed in package.json).
# Everything below the backend blocks applies to every backend.
#
# Under `vite dev` / `vite preview` these are read from .env. A production Node
# build (`npm start`) and Docker read PUBLIC_* from the real process environment
# instead — set them on your deploy platform, not in a shipped .env.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ===========================================================================
# Backend — pick one
#
# The backend is whichever @misiki/*-connector package.json installs; there is
# no file in the repo to edit and nothing to uncomment in kitcommerce.config.ts.
# Uncomment exactly one block below, matching the connector you installed.
# init.ts throws at boot when a block belonging to a different backend is set.
#
# PUBLIC_CONNECTOR overrides the detection. Set it to attach a connector this
# repo has never heard of, or to choose when several are installed:
#
#   PUBLIC_CONNECTOR='@my-co/custom-connector'
# ===========================================================================

# --- Litekart (default) ----------------------------------------------------
# @misiki/litekart-connector · docs/LITEKART.md
PUBLIC_LITEKART_API_URL='https://api.litekart.in'
PUBLIC_LITEKART_DOMAIN='arialshop.com'
# Store to serve when the domain can't be resolved to one (required in Docker/production).
# PUBLIC_LITEKART_STORE_ID=''

# --- Medusa ----------------------------------------------------------------
# @misiki/medusa-connector · docs/MEDUSA.md
# PUBLIC_MEDUSA_API_URL='https://next.medusajs.com'
# PUBLIC_MEDUSA_PUBLISHABLE_API_KEY=''
# PUBLIC_MEDUSA_REGION_ID=''

# --- Vendure ---------------------------------------------------------------
# @misiki/vendure-connector · docs/VENDURE.md
# The GraphQL endpoint is resolved as <PUBLIC_VENDURE_API_URL>/shop-api.
# PUBLIC_VENDURE_API_URL='http://localhost:3000'

# --- Saleor ----------------------------------------------------------------
# @misiki/saleor-connector · docs/SALEOR.md
# PUBLIC_SALEOR_API_URL='https://store.saleor.cloud/graphql/'


# ===========================================================================
# Backend — the other 22 connectors
#
# Same deal: install the package, uncomment its block. These need no extra
# wiring — src/lib/core/connectors/init.ts derives the prefix from the
# connector name (`x-cart` -> PUBLIC_X_CART_*) and hands every variable under
# it to the connector, camelCased, so PUBLIC_SPRYKER_ANONYMOUS_CUSTOMER_ID
# arrives as `anonymousCustomerId` with nothing here knowing that key exists.
# A connector this repo has never heard of is configured the same way.
#
# A backend that answers no CORS (GoCommerce is one) also takes
# PUBLIC_<NAME>_PROXY_PATH='/backend': its connector then calls /backend/* on
# this origin, and src/hooks.server.ts forwards that to PUBLIC_<NAME>_API_URL,
# in dev and production alike.
#
# A store whose products shoppers design (GoCommerce's customizer) uploads each
# design's print file through that path, up to 15 MB. A production Node build
# refuses request bodies over 512 KB unless BODY_SIZE_LIMIT is raised; set
# BODY_SIZE_LIMIT='16M' in the server's environment.
#
# A store closed behind a password (GoCommerce D170) gets 20 tries an hour per
# shopper, counted by the engine against the address this server forwards. Behind
# a CDN or proxy, set ADDRESS_HEADER and XFF_DEPTH (adapter-node) so the server
# knows that address, accept traffic only from that proxy, and list this server
# in the engine's GOCOMMERCE_TRUSTED_PROXIES. Without them every shopper counts
# as this server, and one person's wrong tries lock everyone out for an hour.
#
# One deployment can serve every store of a GoCommerce platform:
# PUBLIC_GOCOMMERCE_BASE_DOMAIN='shopnx.in' makes a request for acme.shopnx.in
# sell for store `acme`, and a subdomain the engine has no store for renders
# this storefront's own 404 page. src/hooks.server.ts hands the connector the
# request host it needs for that.
#
# PUBLIC_WEB_OTP='true' lets Chrome on Android fill the sign-in code in from the
# text. Turn it on only once the SMS template ends with "@<site> #<code>"
# (GoCommerce's web_otp variable); until then Chrome asks the shopper to allow
# it and then reads nothing.
#
# Four backends keep their own statics instead of the shared credentials hook
# (Vendure, Medusa, Saleor, Shopify); those are handled in init.ts already.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Bagisto ---------------------------------------------------------------
# @misiki/bagisto-connector · docs/BAGISTO.md
# Already read by the /proxy/bagisto/* route, which forwards to this base URL.
# PUBLIC_BAGISTO_API_URL='https://demo.bagisto.com'

